PL/SQL is Oracle's procedural extension of SQL: it adds variables, loops, conditions, procedures, functions, triggers and packages that run inside the database.
```sql
BEGIN
  FOR r IN (SELECT name, salary FROM emp WHERE salary > 50000) LOOP
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(r.name || ' earns ' || r.salary);
  END LOOP;
END;
/
```
